  abstract = {We present an operator--analytic framework connecting the Weil criterion for the Riemann Hypothesis with the geometry of a functional manifold associated with the zeta function.~Through a sequence of analytic modules (T{$_0$}--A{$_3$}--RKHS--T{$_5$}), the positivity of the quadratic form Q({$\Phi$}) is extended from compact subspaces to the full Weil class, establishing global non-negative curvature on the functional sphere of {$\zeta$}(s) with the critical line Re(s)=1/2 as the unique geodesic of zero curvature.~The proof is entirely analytic, self-contained, and modular.},
